    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The NASA G-III Meteorological and Navigation Data NURTURE dataset contains information recorded by the onboard navigation and data collection systems of the NASA G-III research aircraft. In addition to typical navigation data (e.g. date, time, latitude/longitude, and altitude), it also contains outside meteorological parameters such as wind speed, wind direction, and temperature. These data were collected during the North American Upstream Feature-Resolving and Tropopause Uncertainty Reconnaissance Experiment (NURTURE) field campaign. The NURTURE campaign is focused on quantifying the impact that perturbations poleward of the jet stream have on jet stream variability and high impact weather events. NURTURE will provide the first mesoscale observations of antecedent tropopause structure and near-jet environment that lead to high impact weather events. NURTURE will target tropopause polar vortices, dynamics supporting jet superpositions, mesoscale stratosphere-troposphere interactions, and diabatic processes (ESPO 2026). The NURTURE G-III meteorological and navigation dataset files are available from January 24, 2026, through February 19, 2026, in ICARTT format. This is an ASCII format with metadata requirements.",
